{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact local LC-1 head 16d95752889dced2602c91f81707a8e3b02b7291, tree 8dbd28f7fca3b72147b29275d1932f74a65935fa, on builder/lc1-lending-counter-releases-20261114, all seven artifacts, for request 66344ab8 under implementation promise e380f820 and my promise 69662521. I read the head from the shared object store. The branch is not on origin. LC-1 does what request 91829f2e asks and nothing more.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Packets. `examples/lending/releases/0.2.0/application.dap.json` is blob e4e43a01, and `apps/counter/releases/0.2.0/application.dap.json` is blob 22a65663. These are the exact blobs of `examples/lending/application.dap.json` and `apps/counter/application.dap.json` on the planner's packet branch at 64d3d6c1. The head only moves them under their version. Both authored configurations still say version 0.2.0 at this head.\n- Formatter. `CANONICAL_PROTOCOL_PACKETS` adds the two paths, and `format-json.test.mjs` asserts that the formatter selects neither path. The packet bytes therefore stay the signed bytes.\n- Rows. `APPLICATION_TRUST` in `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc` holds two rows: Lending sha256:93819e26… and Counter sha256:f681c1b5…, each with publisher key_qNT9aIt0WhJndvMP7UV33FFJ7DOYwW0JUvOv4PhNlFI and host `github.com`. The release IDs and the publisher equal the planner's signing act 196d99b7. The same file binds `APPLICATION_CONTENT` to `dap-lending-application-content`, in the same form as the Grow, connect and artroom-scope Workers. No other Worker, screen host or install context changes, and `APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS` stays empty.\n- Reader trust. The test reads each packet with `readPublishedApplicationPackage2`, first with no expected digest and then with the row's release. That reader is the install boundary: it verifies the manifest signature against the manifest's publisher key and refuses a release ID that differs from the expected digest. The test then requires the manifest publisher to equal the row's publisher, the host to be `github.com`, each committed packet to name a distinct release, and the set of row releases to equal the set of committed packets. A row without a packet and a packet without a row both fail.\n- Version-aware reproduction. When a packet's manifest version equals the authored version, the packet's entry, definitions, semantic ID and presentation ID must equal the current `release-identifiers.json`, and a difference fails with a message that tells the developer to raise the version in `dap.application.json` and `package.ts`. At this head both versions are 0.2.0, so the check runs for both packets. After C3 raises both to 0.3.0, the 0.2.0 packets keep their signature, release and publisher checks, and the source comparison moves to the new version, as ruling 163de663 intends. The head adds no identifiers copy and no constants module.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-lc1-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 0ad7621f…, as the request states. Its first lines name head faece658 and tree 1f9227af with 0 changed files. It reports Node 195, Counting 55, `scope-scale: omitted-by-gate`, terminal evidence complete for all four stages, and ends \"gate passed\". The stage log shows the reproduction case and the formatter case passing. From faece658 to the head only the implementation note changes.\n- Scope. Main 57f887ce is an ancestor, and origin main is still 57f887ce. The seven artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --name-only 57f887ce 16d95752`. The commit-message check passes: 5 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A signed packet lives under its version, the deployment row names the release and the publisher, and the packet carries its own identifiers. Each fact has one home, and the test joins them through the published reader.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The trust rows admit exactly two releases, each bound to one publisher key, and the reader refuses a packet whose signature or release ID does not match. The content bucket is private and the planner creates it. The rows grant install trust only. No screen host, install context or published route changes, so no new page or tool reaches these releases until their own requests.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One small note: the test strips only whole-line `//` comments from the JSONC file. A trailing comment on a value line would make the parse fail loudly, not pass silently, so it needs no change now.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, bucket creation, deployment, installation or publication. The planner decides the landing. C3 must merge LC-1's landed main before its gate, as the request states.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a91d8e2804780754eb9fafaab39cde18b3d06261","binding":"assigned","head":"16d95752889dced2602c91f81707a8e3b02b7291","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6966252142ca19f5a754fc1f58d57703ba85ad74\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e380f82004841671aef4dbb3a37c5d4b7e5cac80\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6966252142ca19f5a754fc1f58d57703ba85ad74","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:458ab4cc9ace5b829be47f125e14e07cffb7b2e8, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4bfb9b17560966f9101bb2c48440cd8203c8fa6f, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5826ab59a366c4e96e1ed60a50e6129458b3712d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66344ab83d8fc30114b68576e1f2b5ecd2e1a80d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6966252142ca19f5a754fc1f58d57703ba85ad74, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:945ba8a5a95a7db5e9d39620655d0859da752137,